@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Our Zoo";
}

<div class="container">
    <h1>About Zoolirante Zoo</h1>

    <div class="section">
        <p>Zoolirante Zoo is a conservation charity with more than 15,000 members. We are a treasured part of the Australian community, having shared the wonder of wildlife since 2010.</p>

        <h2>Our Purpose</h2>
        <p>Our purpose is to <span class="emphasis">connect people with nature</span> and <span class="emphasis">save species from extinction</span>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Zoolirante City Zoo</h2>
        <p>Where in Australia can you step off a busy city street and in just a few minutes experience the thrill of hand-feeding kangaroos, rubbing shoulders with our native koalas and wombats, hear the roar of an African lion or feel a flutter of wind on your face as a colorful parrot swoops just centimetres above your head? The answer? Zoolirante City Zoo.</p>

        <p>An award-winning, not-for-profit, conservation charity with ZAA accreditation, Zoolirante City Zoo's mission is to connect people with nature and save animals from extinction.</p>

        <p>With over 1,800 animals calling Zoolirante City Zoo home, visitors turn adventurers as they explore their way through our lush botanic gardens, finding themselves within a whisker of our native and exotic animals in natural, unique and stimulating environments. And when it's time to leave? Their minds are filled with new memories and an interest in wildlife conservation firmly planted.</p>

        <p>A green oasis in the heart of the city, no trip to Australia is complete without a visit to the award-winning Zoolirante City Zoo.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Zoolirante Wildlife Park</h2>
        <p>Where else in Australia can you hand-feed endangered species like rhinos, get eye-to-eye with a giraffe, within clawing distance of the most fearsome cats of all, or experience the ultimate heart-racing luxury of arriving at the park via helicopter before enjoying a three course lunch? Answer? Nowhere but Zoolirante Wildlife Park!</p>

        <p>Zoolirante Wildlife Park's vast expanse of Australian bushland is transformed into habitats where giraffe, lion, hyena and even rhinos roam alongside native and endangered animals.</p>

        <p>With more than 60% of the species at Zoolirante Wildlife Park threatened with extinction in the wild, a visit delights, inspires and educates and brings the fight to save animals from extinction to life through innovative experiences, encounters and tours.</p>

        <p>Just one hour from the city, Zoolirante Wildlife Park transports visitors from the hustle of urban life to wild and open spaces.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Animal Welfare</h2>
        <p>Zoolirante City Zoo and Zoolirante Wildlife Park are accredited by the Zoo and Aquarium Association (ZAA) and dedicated to the continuous support of positive animal welfare through a science-based approach.</p>

        <p>We care deeply for all our furry, feathered and scaled friends so when we're talking about welfare, we refer to the different feelings and sensations each animal under our care experiences, ranging from positive to negative, given the conditions in which it lives in.</p>

        <p>Providing exceptional care for our animals is one of our highest priorities at Zoolirante Zoo. We do so using a science-based approach to animal welfare that focuses on the Five Domains: Environment, behaviour, nutrition, health and positive mental state.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Beyond Our Sites</h2>
        <p>Our core business continues to focus on zoo visits and educational services which have transformed to become more adaptive, diverse and interactive. However, Zoolirante Zoo's broader commitment to protecting wildlife has significantly grown as we demonstrate world class zoo standards and contribute to local and global efforts to save species.</p>

        <p>Both Zoolirante City Zoo and Zoolirante Wildlife Park have celebrated outstanding breeding success and our captivating, quirky and unique animals have captured the hearts of our visitors.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Our Approach</h2>
        <p>At the heart of our purpose are a set of principles that guide how we operate:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>The ethical care and welfare of animals is our priority.</li>
            <li>We apply a science-based approach to our conservation work and adopt the highest standards for wildlife health, management and husbandry.</li>
            <li>We are uniquely placed to reach and engage with communities and to grow support for conservation locally, nationally and globally.</li>
            <li>We believe that everyone has a role to play in conservation.</li>
            <li>Through our Reconciliation Action Plan, we are committed to working collaboratively with Indigenous peoples as the traditional custodians of the Country our sites are located on.</li>
            <li>To achieve universal accessibility, we endeavour to engage with all communities and to be diverse, equitable, accessible and inclusive.</li>
            <li>Our aim is to provide visitors with an experience that is enjoyable, safe, accessible and inclusive and inspires positive action for conservation.</li>
            <li>We will apply and showcase sustainable practices in the planning, daily operations and management of our sites.</li>
            <li>Each of us is responsible for providing a safe, positive and enjoyable working environment.</li>
            <li>Our success is influenced by creativity, innovation and the use of technology to adapt and continuously improve.</li>
            <li>Building relationships with like-minded partners, sponsors and donors is vital to our capacity to deliver on our purpose within and beyond our gates.</li>
            <li>We are independent and non-party political.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Zoolirante Strategic Plan</h2>
        <p>Zoolirante Zoo has five Strategic Directions that sets the agenda for what we aim to deliver:</p>

        <ol>
            <li>Achieving positive and impactful outcomes for conservation</li>
            <li>Delivering expertise and excellence in wildlife care and animal welfare</li>
            <li>Connecting with and influencing our audience</li>
            <li>Demonstrating and championing environmental sustainability</li>
            <li>Innovating and growing our organisation</li>
        </ol>

        <p>Zoolirante's Strategic Directions are supported by detailed planning initiatives including our Master Plan and Conservation Directions.</p>
    </div>
</div>